</header><section class="sec" id="services" aria-labelledby="s-t">
  <p class="kick" aria-hidden="true">What we do</p>
  <h2 class="h2" id="s-t">Concrete work, start to finish</h2>
  <div class="svc">
    <article class="svc__it rv"><p class="svc__n">01</p><h3 class="svc__h">Slabs</h3><p class="svc__p">House slabs, shed slabs and floor slabs – formwork, reinforcement and pour to spec.</p></article>
    <article class="svc__it rv"><p class="svc__n">02</p><h3 class="svc__h">Driveways</h3><p class="svc__p">Plain, coloured or exposed aggregate driveways with proper base prep and falls.</p></article>
    <article class="svc__it rv"><p class="svc__n">03</p><h3 class="svc__h">Footings</h3><p class="svc__p">Strip footings, pad footings and pier footings for structures and extensions.</p></article>
    <article class="svc__it rv"><p class="svc__n">04</p><h3 class="svc__h">Exposed Aggregate</h3><p class="svc__p">Decorative exposed aggregate finishes – driveways, paths, patios and pool surrounds.</p></article>
    <article class="svc__it rv"><p class="svc__n">05</p><h3 class="svc__h">Shed & Shed Slabs</h3><p class="svc__p">Farm sheds, garage slabs and workshop floors – level, durable, ready for the kit.</p></article>
    <article class="svc__it rv"><p class="svc__n">06</p><h3 class="svc__h">Paths</h3><p class="svc__p">Garden paths, side access paths and stepping-stone trails – formed and finished clean.</p></article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec sec--panel" id="about" aria-labelledby="a-t">
  <div class="inner">
  <p class="kick" aria-hidden="true">About</p>
  <h2 class="h2" id="a-t">The precision of a finisher,<br>the discipline of the site</h2>
  <div class="about">
    <div class="about__art rv">
      <img src="assets/dm-gal1.jpg" alt="Concrete slab being finished on site – DM Concreting" width="1400" height="1000" loading="lazy">
      <p class="about__cap">// ON THE TOOLS – slabs, driveways, footings, exposed aggregate</p>
    </div>
    <ul class="about__lis">
      <li class="rv">Every pour gets the same layout lines, screed rails and finish passes – from a garden path to a house slab, a shed floor to a driveway.</li>
      <li class="rv">Working clean is non-negotiable: formwork square, reinforcement placed, joints tooled, site left ready for the next trade.</li>
      <li class="rv">Clear scopes before work starts – you know what is being poured, with what mix, and what it will take.</li>
      <li class="rv">Local to the Hunter. Owner-operator Dan Miles, on the tools, accountable for the finish.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  </div>
</section>

